To coordinate cooperative threads without busy-waiting (CPU spinning), Java provides wait(), notify(), and notifyAll() on java.lang.Object.
Producer-Consumer Model Example:
class Buffer {
    private int data;
    private boolean available = false;
    public synchronized void produce(int val) throws InterruptedException {
        while (available) wait(); // Wait if buffer is full
        data = val; available = true;
        System.out.println('Produced: ' + val);
        notifyAll(); // Wake up consumers
    }
    public synchronized int consume() throws InterruptedException {
        while (!available) wait(); // Wait if buffer is empty
        available = false;
        System.out.println('Consumed: ' + data);
        notifyAll(); // Wake up producers
        return data;
    }
}
